        "id": 1040080
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-23T23:01:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Added comments in named_attr_update() on how a size change goes through the\nsame read-modify-write as a WRITE.",
      "parentUuid": "3e42b5e2_88d58eea",
      "revId": "dc6bb83c6feca2cf06aba4658308c2980496c745",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f1de969_bac5f0be",
        "filename": "src/FSAL/FSAL_VFS/namedattr.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1257,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T23:58:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this per RFC that any setattr other than size is ignored and doesn\u0027t cause an error?",
      "revId": "dc6bb83c6feca2cf06aba4658308c2980496c745",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4dbaada5_9f04f8de",
        "filename": "src/FSAL/FSAL_VFS/namedattr.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1257,
      "author": {
        "id": 1040080
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-23T23:01:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, it isn\u0027t per RFC. RFC 8881 5.3 only says named attributes needn\u0027t\nsupport as many attributes as other objects, and nfs4_op_setattr() tells the\nclient every requested attribute was set, so ignoring them claimed changes\nthat didn\u0027t happen. It now returns NFS4ERR_ATTRNOTSUPP for anything but\nsize. Before changing it I checked that macOS 27 never sets other attributes\non a named attribute: setting, overwriting, listing and removing xattrs,\ncp -p, ditto, touch, chmod and mv.",
      "parentUuid": "7f1de969_bac5f0be",
      "revId": "dc6bb83c6feca2cf06aba4658308c2980496c745",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8548cab9_1a60e0ca",
        "filename": "src/FSAL/FSAL_VFS/namedattr.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003571
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-21T23:58:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is this non-support a problem? We COULD make a copy of the named attribute on link.",
      "revId": "dc6bb83c6feca2cf06aba4658308c2980496c745",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bbcca874_12a05143",
        "filename": "src/FSAL/FSAL_VFS/namedattr.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 1305,
      "author": {
        "id": 1040080
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-10-23T23:01:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d rather leave it as NOTSUPP. This is to support macOS, whose xattr API\nhas no way to link or rename an attribute, so it never sends either. The RFC\ndoesn\u0027t forbid LINK or RENAME within the same named attribute directory, but\nLinux xattrs can\u0027t do either properly: a link would need two names sharing\none value (a copy would give two independent values), and a rename would be\na setxattr then a removexattr, which isn\u0027t atomic. I also checked FreeBSD,\nwhich added named attributes in 15: its linkat() refuses to link a named attribute, but it does allow renaming a named attribute within its directory, so that will fail against Ganesha. I\u0027ve put this in a comment in namedattr.c.",
      "parentUuid": "8548cab9_1a60e0ca",
      "revId": "dc6bb83c6feca2cf06aba4658308c2980496c745",
      "serverId": "d5d70762-12d0-45a1-890d-524b12d3f735"
    }
